  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file set required for the dependency-graph analysis.\n\n**Detection chain traced:**\n- Spring Boot's `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` (in `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java`) gates activation on `ClassUtils.isPresent(\"org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory\", \u2026)` \u2014 a hard-coded string check against `log4j-core`'s `Log4jContextFactory`, registered via `spring.factories` (`LoggingSystemFactory`).\n- `LoggingSystemFactory` / `LoggingSystem.get()` load all factories through `SpringFactoriesLoader`, with `LoggingApplicationListener` (note: lives in `org.springframework.boot.context.logging`, not `org.springframework.boot.logging` \u2014 a package that moved in the 2.4 restructuring) driving `beforeInitialize()`/`initialize()`.\n- On the Log4j2 side, `log4j-to-slf4j`'s `SLF4JProvider` binds the Log4j2 API to SLF4J using the programmatic `Provider(priority, versions, loggerContextFactoryClass, threadContextMapClass)` constructor rather than a `META-INF/log4j-provider.properties` file (confirmed absent at that path) \u2014 `ProviderUtil` loads providers via `ServiceLoader`/classpath scan for `Provider` implementations.\n- `Provider.java` (log4j-api) is the base class whose constructor shape is what changed between major versions \u2014 this is the load-bearing symbol for the bridge restructuring since it governs how `log4j-to-slf4j` self-registers.\n\nThese 10 files give the full picture: Spring Boot's classpath-presence detection \u2192 log4j-core's `Log4jContextFactory` \u2192 log4j-api's `Provider`/`ProviderUtil` SPI \u2192 log4j-to-slf4j's `SLF4JProvider` binding.",
